	(text "The bank is the soft start for all the motor capacitance: BMS sees no inrush. Reset closes it, loop open drops it. No software in the path. Compute is not behind it.\nRs 0.5 mOhm: limit 97-123 A (VCL 48.5-61.5 mV), breaker 160-260 A (VCB 80-130 mV). Above peak draw and JK DOC 80 A. 1.8 W at 60 A.\nStart: Cdv 100 nF, gate 10-22 uA, 100-220 V/s, 0.25-0.55 s to full. Bus ceiling 9.4 mF at 2.06 A hot DC SOA line (112 W, 45 K Tj rise). Drive caps unmeasured.\nPower limit 652 W at 54.6 V, 480-810 W with tolerance: RPWR = 1.3e5 x Rs x (P - 1.18 mV x VDS / Rs), SNVS452G eq 10, VSNS 6 mV over the 5 mV floor. Timer 4.7 nF: 0.22 ms typ, 0.15-0.39 ms.\nFault check: 810 W is 14.8 A at 54.6 V for up to 0.39 ms. Reviewers read about 16 A at 0.82 ms, 70 C, one FET; TI scales as t^0.346, so about 20.7 A at 0.39 ms: 1.4 x. Read the real curve at layout.\nFETs: 0.85 mOhm for the pair, 5.2 W hot at 60 A, 1.3 W at 30 A, the same again in bank A. UVLO low sinks the gate at 2 mA: about 170 us off.\nThe 2 mA also pulls VBUS down through U1's OUT-GATE zener, against the 54 uA of its internal 1 MOhm SENSE-OUT path, so VBUS reads near 0 V with the banks open.\nBody diodes of both banks pass regen back to the pack with the banks open. OVLO tied low: opening on overvoltage would strand regen on the bus.\nLM5069-1 latches on a fault. Clear: E-stop cycle, then reset.\nBAT spike: the absorber in blocks 10 and 10d (6 x 47 uF) takes the lead current when a bank opens fast, 5.0SMDJ58A is the backstop. FETs and U1 are 100 V.\nPolarity (rev B5): one soldered 8 AWG pigtail pair, side by side, to an XT90 that only mates the pack's XT90S one way (Joey: the pack run is the heaviest connector run in the robot). Nothing on the main path blocks a reversed pack: both banks' body diodes would conduct and D1 becomes the crowbar, so the keyed plug and the bring-up polarity check carry it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 300 92 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a63ce4ec-9f98-5f3c-bebf-0f66b4ad33af")
	)
