	(text "Two Arcol HS50 20R J in parallel, 10 Ohm total, one on each gusset (+X: J3/J4; -X: J25/J26, block 10c; place all four on the board's top edge, +X half, because the -X leads cross under the board, about 150 mm longer), on the 5 mm countersunk Al plates with thermal compound. Each lead pair is twisted. At the 56.8 V threshold: 5.7 A, 322 W total, 2.84 A and 161 W per resistor. MBRS3100 carries the lead and winding inductance at turn-off, so lead length sets EMI, not FET stress. Each is rated 50 W only on Arcol's 535 cm2 plate, so it works on burst energy: 32 g each, about 29 J/K, so a 3 kJ burst is about +50 C per body. Software caps braking at 50 W average over 60 s and 3 kJ per burst, total. Thermostats: one 67L120 under each body, both in series in the E-stop loop (rev B5), so an open resistor can't leave the other unwatched. Threshold values are rev A's, unchanged.\nSelf-powered: VCTL lives as long as the bus or the pack does. If the FET sticks on, the resistor's thermostat opens the loop and the bank drops the bus.\nTLV1805 drives the FET directly: 100 mA peak, 0.3 us into 4 nF. Rev A's driver, meter, shunt, status FET and NTC are gone, and a smaller FET replaces the IPT015.\nLeg stage later: fit 2 Ohm and recheck this FET, 29 A gives about 5 W."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 355.6 280 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e612ced1-99a2-51e6-b92f-cb3a4a85b871")
	)
	(text "4. Bus capacitors"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 355.6 308 0)
