	(text "Ahead of the E-stop: motors off, compute stays up. Soft start in block 5a; the converter's negative-logic ON/OFF is held off until U7's PGD is good (block 10).\nOff board on the top front rail (frame 3877317), baseplate down, 4x M3 into its threaded baseplate (50.8 x 15.24 mm, 3 mm max depth). J24 sits on the board's top edge, -X half. -Vin and -Vout both go to GND: the robot has one ground, P-.\nPigtail about 150 mm, twisted pairs, 18 AWG: 2 wires each way on the input, 3 each way on +12 V (0.1 V drop at 12 A including contacts). At the converter end: 47 uF 100 V aluminium (its ESR damps the lead, 75-150 nH) plus 1 uF across +VIN/-VIN at the pins. 300 W, 25 A, 94.6 %: about 9 W at the 140 W ceiling, into the plate.\nInput UVLO 32-36 V on, 30-34 V off, fixed on the DVE: near an empty pack under sag, compute can drop before the BMS cuts out.\nINA228 addresses, no strap on SDA: L arm 0x40, R arm 0x41, aux 0x43, L leg 0x44, R leg 0x45, SPARE_SW 0x47, waist 0x4C, 12 V 0x4D, MID 0x4F. Powered by the Pi's 3.3 V; Pi pull-ups on I2C."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 424 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "757bfdd4-bc94-57d1-9e16-e874db2a1810")
	)
	(text "5a. Brick soft start (ahead of the E-stop switch)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 440 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "34b06274-793c-569b-aee2-fb4ed7eb6ebd")
	)
