	(text "Own driver: a FET usually dies shorted gate to drain, which would pull a shared gate net to the pack and hold the other bank on. RUN is the only shared signal, and\neach bank takes it through its own diode.\nBoth banks face the same way, drains toward the pack, so regen stays open. Bank B keeps U1, the shunt and the soft start.\nClose order: U8 FLT holds U1 UVLO low (about 1.9 V, through BAT46W + 10k) until BST is up (about 57 ms typ, 35-115 ms with 2.2 uF), so A closes first by logic, not\nby timing. The diode only lets FLT pull down: a failed-high FLT can't enable B. A closes onto MID only. FLT also blocks B if U8 has no charge pump or has tripped.\nOff edge: EN falls first, 4.6 us typ, 6.5 us max, then G1PD pulls 390 nC through 22R: about 2-3 us. On a bus short U1's breaker can open B first, so the spike can\nland on MID with A on: the absorber (block 10) bounds BAT, and so MID, and U17 has its own clamp.\nShort-circuit comparator on RS1: 40.2k gives 99 mV, 158-242 A, above U1's limit. CS+/CS- through 0R with a DNP cap: TI's RC placeholder against nuisance trips. TMR\n100k only (C29 DNP): fastest response, 4.3 us, still latch-off, cleared by an E-stop cycle. It covers reset with B shorted: A opens, and FLT holds B off.\nDriver off holds gate to source with no path to GND, so MID can be biased: 47k + 47k, 0.47 x pack nominal, 0.6 mA, 16 mW each. Hot FET leakage (200 uA per bank at\n125 C) moves MID by up to about 4 V. U17 reads MID through 33k with a 68 V zener at the pin (85 V max): calibrate the 3 % gain.\nSelf-test before reset, pack 36-54.6 V, BMS telemetry for pack voltage: MID 0.33-0.60 x pack and VBUS under 3 V is healthy (U11 reads V_L1: use the highest limb\nmeter). MID within 2 V of pack: A shorted. MID under 3 V: B shorted. VBUS high: both shorted, or the bus has not bled down yet, about 11 s on board caps, longer with\ndrives.\nU17 reads MID on its VBUS pin, and clamp duty on IN+ (block 10d). VBUS alone cannot see one shorted bank, which is why MID is read."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
