		(uuid "d65e6778-fc8e-5acf-bbc6-70fa111d7542")
	)
	(text "Block 10. Absorber: a bank trip into a bus short cuts 350-890 A. tools/absorber_sim.py (pack 54.6 V, no pack yet), worst corners: 0.05 Ohm pulse loop (cell AC resistance),\n0.5-1 uH, D1 at 71.2 V, C -20 %, trip 8.8-17.5 us. Six 47 uF 80 V hybrids (EEH-ZC1K470P, the bus-cap part) give BAT 79 V or less: every can stays under its 80 V rating (rev\nB5: the APZ 100 V line is obsolete). Measure lead L and pulse R at bring-up. 100k bleeds it. BMS close drives about 300 A into three cans for a few us: bench it on the JK.\nU2 feed: F1, 22R, ES1D in series, then 1 uF. A shorted U2 puts the pack on VCTL: 22R holds it to about 1.6 A, so SMAJ15A clamps under 19.2 V (Q6 gate 20 V) and F1 (50 A\nbreaking) opens. The series diode keeps C5 from back-driving U2 when BAT collapses, and 22R keeps C39's inrush far under F1's I2t.\nAbsorber close option (M3), DNP: if the JK trips when it closes onto C38, remove the 0R and fit 2R + the delayed NMOS + its RC: 25 A at close, clamp unchanged\n(absorber_sim.py).\nRUN_A and RUN_B diodes: a U1 pin 2-3 bridge or an EN fault can't drive RUN. FLT reaches UVLO through BAT46W + 10k (2010) with a 12 V zener on FLT_A: FLT low holds UVLO near\n1.9 V; a bridged UVLO puts at most 5.5 mA into FLT and 12.7 V on it (15 V recommended).\nConverter: F2 20 A on the board end protects the pigtail (U7 already limits at 9.7-12.3 A; F2 backs up a shorted Q7). The DVE has no reverse protection, so the keyed connector\ncarries polarity. U7 PGD high (good) turns on the 2N7002, which pulls ON/OFF to -Vin through 220R: on (0.45 V at 2 mA). 220R limits a pin 5-11 short to 55 mA. 470k and the 12\nV zener bias the gate from BRK_IN, so it doesn't depend on VCTL.\n1 uF on RST_SRC (M8): a reset held at power-up no longer arms the latch (tools/latch_sim.py, 36 cases). Reset interlock (M1): Q10 shorts RST_SRC until MID is over about 11 V\n(10 V zener, Q11), and Q14 shorts it while VBUS is over 6-8.5 V (5.1 V zener, hFE spread). Operator rule: wait for VBUS under 3 V. Reset needs MID healthy and the bus down, so\na shorted B can't be hard-closed onto a charged bus. After a stop, wait for the drives' caps to bleed. It loads MID by about 30 uA. 33k on U17 VBUS (M13). 22 nF SRC to GND,\nTI's recommendation for U8. BAT46W (M4). 330 uF on +12V: spare-output shorts and servo back-feed (M9) land in it and the compute loads."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
