	(text "Fifth 47 uF 80 V hybrid on VBUS (EEH-ZC1K470P, active line; the APZ 68 uF is obsolete): 235 uF in all, the value tools/port_sim.py uses.\nSecond SK810L beside D7: the unread forward curve at 300-900 A was worth up to 8 V on BAT at 30 mOhm (absorber_sim D7 sweep, 94 V); two in parallel halve it, so the worst\ncorner stays at about 91 V, as with the assumed 10 mOhm.\nClamp duty: CL_OUT (0/12.1 V) through 100k/1k into U17 IN+ (IN- on GND): 120 mV at 100 % duty, 4.7 ms RC. The Pi reads duty x 120 mV and integrates duty x VBUS^2 / 10 Ohm\nfor the brake-energy cap.\n1 uF 100 V at Q6/D4. GND test points, one per quadrant, and pads on GATE, GATE_A, UVLO, FLT_A for the close-order scope test."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 840 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "708b3116-a044-5ae3-a198-92559050a118")
	)
	(text "6a. Limb port breakers: TPS48111-Q1 + one FET per port, latch-off, enabled by RUN"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 850 22 0)
		(effects
