	)
	(text "The Pi toggles WD_FEED from its control loop (software, not a PWM peripheral) every 50-100 ms; the watchdog wants a falling edge at WDI at least every 270 ms (CWD 3.3 nF C0G: 77.4 x C + 55\nms = 310 ms typ, 270-355 ms with the +-9.5 % timer and 5 % cap band). Miss it and WDO goes low for 200 ms: the NPN in Q5's emitter turns off, the seal-in breaks and RUN falls like a loop\nopen. The latch stays off after WDO releases: only a reset press re-arms it.\nFail-safe: the NPN only conducts while the watchdog's own rail (3.3 V zener from VCTL, not the Pi) feeds its base through 22k and WDO is released. Pi dead, unpowered, rebooting, hung or its\npin floating (100k pull-down): no edges, no latch. Watchdog rail lost: no base drive, no latch. It sits in series, so it can only drop the latch, never hold it (a shorted NPN just removes\nthe watchdog).\nWhile the Pi stays dead the watchdog repeats 310 ms released / 200 ms low; a reset press in a released window closes the latch until the next low, under 0.36 s, with no drive commands (the\nPi is dead). The first 0.3 s after VCTL comes up the watchdog is released before its first timeout.\nSoftware requirement: drive CanTimeout set and read back before every enable."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 450 700 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8ebbfb4b-e91a-517a-9b7a-8b0598cf7fa7")
	)
